+## Item stack minimum 100 candidate
+
+October17 read-only OVH audit found 20,490 already-stackable definitions below
+100, including 6,734 tradeskill materials. The candidate changes only
+items.stacksize to 100 for stackable=1 and stacksize<100. Preserve existing
+100/larger limits, nonstackables, charges, recipes, prices and player inventory.
+Leather Padding16488 goes50→100; ore10500, water13006 and bandages13009 go20→100.
+Existing stacks can be merged after activation; no automatic consolidation.
+
+Source: E:/EQ_Local_Dev/_worktrees/item-stacks-100, based on origin/main a59974d.
+`tools/item_stack_sizes.py` generates guarded transactional SQL from exact ID/
+old-limit preimages. `tools/tests/test_item_stack_sizes.py` has three checks;
+`tools/tests/rehearse_item_stack_sizes.py` passes nine actual MariaDB temporary-
+table cases including the complete candidate set, drift, repeated execution
+and post-update failure rollback. The existing25 native tradeskill tests pass;
+independent review found no blockers. Rehearsal compares six item columns,
+not a full-cache comparison; current schema has no automatic/generated fields.
+
+`docs/ops/item-stacks-100-20261017/{README.md,rehearsal.json,verification.json}`
+records scope and exact owner QA. Production SQL, main promotion, cache reload,
+wiki publication and gameplay acceptance remain pending. No native/client/ABI
+change: use current shared_memory and a controlled whole-game restart to load
+the changed item definitions. Rules/quest reload is insufficient. Preserve all
+current cache policies and other native releases. After possible player access,
+retain the higher limits; never lower them under owned stacks or restore player
+snapshots. Any pre-access inverse needs fresh afterimage checks and cache reload.
